%I A401495 #5 Nov 03 2026 17:02:27
%S A401495 1,2,4,11,26,90,230,707,1591,3804,9438,26326,64544,201696
%N A401495 Number of unlabeled Riordan graphs on n vertices whose complement is also a Riordan graph.
%C A401495 Riordan graphs are defined in A401493. A graph is counted if both it and its complement admit a Riordan labeling, possibly different ones.
%C A401495 The number of self-complementary Riordan graphs on n vertices, for n = 1..14, is 1, 0, 0, 1, 2, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 2, 2, 0.
%C A401495 a(1)-a(10) agree with an exhaustive test of all graphs on n vertices.
%H A401495 Gi-Sang Cheon, Ji-Hwan Jung, Sergey Kitaev and Seyed Ahmad Mojallal, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.laa.2019.05.033">Riordan graphs I: Structural properties</a>, Linear Algebra Appl. 579 (2019), 89-135.
%H A401495 Arnauld Mesinga Mwafise, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23676628">riordan-graph-enumerator</a>, C++ software for enumerating, listing and sampling Riordan graphs, Zenodo, 2026.
%e A401495 a(5) = 26: of the 30 Riordan graphs on 5 vertices (A401493), exactly 4 have a non-Riordan complement, namely the complements of the 4 non-Riordan graphs listed in A401493.
%Y A401495 Cf. A000088, A401493, A401496.
%K A401495 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A401495 1,2
%A A401495 _Arnauld Mesinga Mwafise_, Oct 27 2026
